Subject: [PATCH] em: per-message traces from the journal to em's debug channel

em_ctrl's journal is capped by the image (LogRateLimitBurst 1000 per 30 s). Through a room
catalog on rdk-1004 (6 October 2026) em_ctrl wrote 2,500 to 8,500 lines per 30 s: journald
dropped 1,468 to 7,506 of them in every window, the evidence the lab's tools read from it
(the native backhaul lines, renewals, validation failures) among them. About 70 % of what
it kept were traces of per-message work: an unknown IE per station capability, the
operating class table at each update, the topology tree's search at each Topology Response,
each radio's state per orchestration step, the steps of each candidate query and each
backhaul STA capability exchange, every 1905 ACK sent.

Those 67 statements now print through em_util_dbg_print: nothing unless em's per-module
debug switch is present (/nvram/emCtrlDbg for the controller's own code, /nvram/emConfDbg
for the code it shares with the agent), then to /tmp/emCtrl or /tmp/emConf as before for
em's debug output. What stays on the journal: errors and validation failures, one line per
Topology Response and Notification received, each candidate query sent and its result, the
native backhaul module's lines.

Upstream-Status: Pending

